  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a matrix <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>&#945;</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>&#946;</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>&#947;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>&#947;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></math>&nbsp;are three distinct natural numbers.<br />If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>det</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>adj</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>adj</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>adj</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>adj</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>16</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>16</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>16</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>32</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>16</mn></msup></math>, then the number of such&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>- tuples <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is _______.",
